=== Psalm 46
--- Psalm 46 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalm 46
sub: A very present help in trouble
refs: Psalm 46:1

--- Our refuge and strength
kicker: Psalm 46 · A very present help
big: Psalm 46:1
p: The opening verse of **Psalm 46** is a wonderful text on the faithfulness and protection of God. It has been preached on an untold number of times, been made a life-verse for scores of people, been pinned to walls, stuck on refrigerators, is a prominent part of hundreds of thousands of devotionals, verse of the days, and used in countless facebook memes.
p: What a comfort for believers in trouble these words have been and continue to be.

--- Therefore will not we fear
kicker: Psalm 46 · Our fortress
scripture: Psalm 46:2-3 | mark: Therefore will not we fear
p: Again and again, the Bible tells us that God is our refuge and strength. Our buckler, our fortress, our shield and strong tower. The promise of protection extended to the children of God is found throughout the word, and ultimately the entire Bible is a promise of deliverance from a holy and merciful God.
p: The Gospel itself is the promise of protection and life, from God to all who come to Him. And the promise is kept in the Son, the Lord Christ Jesus.

--- God is in the midst of her
kicker: Psalm 46 · Very present
scripture: Psalm 46:4-7 | mark: God is in the midst of her; The LORD of hosts is with us
p: He is our rock. He is our strong foundation. He is the gathering hen, protecting her chicks under her wing. He is the Good Shepherd, watching over the flock, His love for His sheep so deep, that He laid down His life for us.
p: God is very present, always with us, desiring to be our Comfort, to be involved in our lives, and our shelter in the time of storm.
p: And in any Christian life, given enough time, this is proven to us again and again.

--- My refuge and my fortress
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 46:1
big: Psalm 91:2 | mark: He is my refuge and my fortress
big: Proverbs 18:10 | mark: a strong tower
big: Psalm 18:2 | mark: my high tower

--- He shall preserve thy soul
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 46:1
big: Psalm 121:7
big: Deuteronomy 31:6 | mark: he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee
big: 2 Thessalonians 3:3 | mark: the Lord is faithful

--- A strong hold in the day of trouble
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 46:1
big: Isaiah 41:10 | mark: I will help thee
big: Psalm 34:17 | mark: delivereth them out of all their troubles
big: Nahum 1:7 | mark: a strong hold in the day of trouble

--- Be still, and know
kicker: Psalm 46 · The Lord of hosts is with us
scripture: Psalm 46:8-11 | mark: Be still, and know that I am God
p: These are not platitudes or empty promises. These are real and observable and heartfelt understandings and expressions of faith, forged in troubled times.
p: God so loved the world that He gave His only begotten Son to keep this promise. God commanded His love towards us that while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.
p: We know, by the testifying of the Holy Spirit inside of us, that Spirit of adoption, that we are the Father's and His children are protected.

=== Psalm 47
--- Psalm 47 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalm 47
sub: A great King over all the earth
refs: Psalm 47:1

--- A great King over all the earth
kicker: Psalm 47 · Shout unto God
scripture: Psalm 47:1-2 | mark: he is a great King over all the earth
p: **Psalm 47** is a song of praise for the Lord, the King of kings. Christ Jesus, Who shall put every nation under His feet.

--- The kingdoms of this world
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 47:2
scripture: Revelation 11:15-17 | mark: The kingdoms of this world are become the kingdoms of our Lord, and of his Christ

--- He shall choose our inheritance
kicker: Psalm 47 · The nations under our feet
scripture: Psalm 47:3-4 | mark: He shall choose our inheritance for us
p: He shall rule and reign with a rod of iron, and give to all His people their inheritance in His Kingdom.

--- God is gone up with a shout
kicker: Psalm 47 · The sound of a trumpet
big: Psalm 47:5
p: Jesus is God. Verse 5 says *God is gone up with a shout, the LORD with the sound of a trumpet.* A prophetic Old Testament verse, made clear in the New Testament, carrying the comfort of all believers;
scripture: 1 Thessalonians 4:16-17 | mark: with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God

--- Sing praises
kicker: Psalm 47 · Sing praises unto our King
big: Psalm 47:6
p: We shall sing of the glories of the Lord, forever.
scripture: Revelation 7:10-12 | mark: Salvation to our God which sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb

--- King of kings
kicker: Psalm 47 · The King of all the earth
scripture: Psalm 47:7-8 | mark: For God is the King of all the earth
big: Revelation 19:16
p: For Jesus is the King of all the earth, and reigns over the heathen. All the nations. He is greatly exalted above every name.

--- Every knee should bow
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 47:9
scripture: Philippians 2:9-11 | mark: That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow

--- He is greatly exalted
kicker: Psalm 47 · The shields of the earth
big: Psalm 47:9 | mark: he is greatly exalted
p: Jesus will reign over all things, and, having defeated death and been made ruler of all, He will give all to God the Father. A perfect sacrifice, holy and acceptable, made holy by His righteousness:

--- Then cometh the end
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 47:9
scripture: 1 Corinthians 15:24-27 | mark: For he must reign, till he hath put all enemies under his feet
p: **Psalm 47** is a wonderful and prophetic song of praise and worship for the Kingdom of God, under our Lord Christ Jesus. All honor and praise is His. Amen

